**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests`

**How to implement.** The home of the one item-model evaluator, and the values it reads (001 §N 'One item-model evaluator, ItemModel × parameters × orientation × λ → MuellerMatrix'; 001 §I: `Parameter` = a name plus a `ParameterState`; step 214: 'a kind's range is its model's (S8.1)'). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs`: `module ItemEvaluation` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `MuellerInverse.fs`, the last Domain file, because the evaluator calls `MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:retarderMueller`) and `MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward` (`MuellerInverse.fs:createBerremanForward`): one `<Compile Include="ItemEvaluation.fs" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines: the item-model evaluator, model × parameters × orientation × λ (spec 0050 S8.1). It opens `ItemModels` and `Kit`; each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (2) `ItemEvaluationError`, an `*Error` union whose cases are `MissingParameterValueErr of reason : string` (the values hold no number for a parameter the model publishes, naming it) and `ParameterOutOfRangeErr of reason : string` (a value outside its kind's range, naming the parameter, the value and the range). `member this.describe : string` renders them `the values hold no number for the parameter: <reason>` and `the parameter value is outside its range: <reason>`. Later steps add their own cases with their renderings. (3) `ParameterValues` = `ParameterValues of Map<ParameterName, ParameterValue>`, the numbers an evaluation reads, by name. `static member ofParameters (parameters : Parameter list) : ParameterValues` takes each parameter's number from its state (step 214): a `KnownParameter` its value, an `UnknownParameter` its `start`, a `CalibratedParameter` its `value`. `static member defaultsOf (axes : ItemParameterAxis list) : ParameterValues` holds each axis's `defaultValue`. `member this.withValue (name : ParameterName) (value : ParameterValue) : ParameterValues` replaces or adds one number. `member this.valueOf (name : ParameterName) : Result<ParameterValue, ItemEvaluationError>` answers it or `MissingParameterValueErr`. `member this.checkedFor (axes : ItemParameterAxis list) : Result<ParameterValues, ItemEvaluationError>` answers the values when every axis has a number within its kind's range and otherwise the first failure in axis order: no number is `MissingParameterValueErr`; a number that is NaN or infinite, a `FractionParameter` outside [0, 1], or a `ScaleParameter` or `ThicknessParameter` below 0 is `ParameterOutOfRangeErr`; an `AngleParameter`, `PhaseParameter`, `MuellerElementParameter` or `ReadingParameter` takes any finite number. Values the axes do not name are kept and ignored. No cache, unit conversion or other member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs`, `module ItemEvaluationTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, opening `OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation`. `parameter values are read from an item's parameter states`: over parameters `a` `KnownParameter 0.1`, `b` an `UnknownParameter` starting at 0.5 within [0, 1] and `c` a `CalibratedParameter` of 0.25 (sigma 0.01, `FitRunName "S@20261101T120000Z"`), `valueOf` answers 0.1, 0.5 and 0.25, and `valueOf` of `d` answers `MissingParameterValueErr` naming `d`. `defaults come from a model's axes and one value can be replaced`: `defaultsOf` of `(OpticalElementModel (RetarderPlateModel ConstantRetardance)).parameterAxes` answers `retardance` π / 2 and `fastAxisOffset` 0, and `withValue ParameterName.retardance` of π / 4 answers π / 4 beside the unchanged offset. `values are checked against a model's axes and their kinds' ranges`: over `SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes` (step 244), the defaults check; `degreeOfPolarization` 1.5 and −0.1, `intensityScale` −1 and an `azimuth` of NaN answer `ParameterOutOfRangeErr` naming the parameter; an `azimuth` of 7 (radians) checks; values without `ellipticity` answer `MissingParameterValueErr` naming it; and over `(BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId).parameterAxes` a `substrate.thickness` of −1e-3 answers `ParameterOutOfRangeErr`. `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct reason renders its text with the reason.

**Acceptance.** After `ItemEvaluation.fs` lands, `ParameterValues` MUST read an item's numbers from its parameter states or a model's defaults and `checkedFor` MUST refuse a missing number or one outside its kind's range with a typed `ItemEvaluationError`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `parameter values are read from an item's parameter states`, `defaults come from a model's axes and one value can be replaced`, `values are checked against a model's axes and their kinds' ranges` and `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.
